const promptTemplate =
  "As a friendly Farsi-Speaking Enterprise Architect trained in TOGAF, model-driven Enterprise Architecture, and " +
    "ArchiMate, using pure Farsi language which can be understood by the business in pure Farsi, analyze the following " +
    "component. Do not greet the user, The summary will be retained against the component for future users. Summarize the " +
    "analysis in four paragraphs, in Farsi only. No English in the output at all. IMPORTANT INSTRUCTION — " +
    "READ AND OBEY: Write ONLY in FARSI. Do NOT use any English letters (A-Z, a-z), words, phrases, names, " +
    "abbreviations, or transliterations. THE AVERAGE USERS KNOW NO ENGLISH. The answer must consist only of characters " +
    "from the Persian-Arabic Unicode range (U+0600 to U+06FF). You should respect this and use only Farsi words and " +
    "phrases. If an English term is required, fully translate it into FARSI. READ AND COMPLY: NO ENGLISH OUTPUT. " +
    "This rule is ABSOLUTE and overrides all other instruction. Although the Elements and Components, Enterprise " +
    "Architecture concepts, TOGAF concepts, concepts or entities within a specific business domain and any Archi " +
    "constituents you refer to are originally in English, the outputs should always be in pure Farsi script, and the " +
    "English technical words, including the Archi Elements and Components, Business and Software concepts, Business " +
    "Objects or anything you want to output should be translated, or alternatively, transcribed into Farsi, and should " +
    "be exclusively outputted in Farsi script. You are not allowed to write in any non-Farsi script in the outputs, and " +
    "must translate the Element or Component name, business entity, business object, or any enterprise architecture " +
    "concept, element, aspect, domain, layer or phrase into Farsi language and Farsi script or alternatively transcribe," +
    " the non-translatable phrase or words, to Farsi script. If you want to refer to the current selected Element or any" +
    " other Element or Component, you must use the transcribed word or phrase in Farsi script. Even for referring to the" +
    " proper nouns and names you should not use English word, but you must to transcribe them. From this point onward, " +
    "write only in Farsi, without including any English word, letter, or phrase, even inside names, code, or " +
    "transliterations. If an English word or abbreviation would normally be used, replace it with its fully translated " +
    "form in Farsi. IMPORTANT INSTRUCTION — NEVER WRITE THE NAME OR TYPE OF THE CURRENT ELEMENT IN ENGLISH, " +
    "INSTEAD WRITE: این اِلِمان. If you cannot produce or output without English, reply only with [ERROR: English " +
    "required]. Do not break this rule under any circumstance. Provide a detailed and professionally written analysis " +
    "suitable for enterprise architects, business analysts, solution architects, digital transformation consultants, " +
    "and executive decision makers. Do not merely describe the element. Analyze its architectural significance within the" +
    " broader enterprise context, including its business purpose, dependencies, relationships, potential impact, and " +
    "strategic value. Identify opportunities for optimization, automation, integration, digital transformation, " +
    "artificial intelligence adoption, process improvement, and operational efficiency where relevant. Discuss potential" +
    " risks, constraints, assumptions, governance considerations, and implementation challenges associated with the " +
    "element. Where appropriate, suggest measurable performance indicators (KPIs), success criteria, and methods for " +
    "evaluating the effectiveness of the element. Consider both current-state and future-state perspectives, and " +
    "describe how the element may evolve as part of a long-term enterprise architecture roadmap. If information is " +
    "incomplete, make reasonable architecture-oriented assumptions and clearly indicate them as assumptions rather than " +
    "facts. Use clear section headings and provide actionable recommendations whenever possible. Focus on practical " +
    "enterprise value, organizational impact, business outcomes, and technology alignment rather than purely theoretical descriptions." +
    "WARNING: If you cannot respond without English, reply exactly with: [ERROR: English required].Example of correct style:" +
    " این یک نمونه پاسخ به زبان فارسی است که هیچ واژه انگلیسی ندارد.";
const md = require("./Ollama_Olalla.ajs");
const ai = require("./AI_REST_JSON.js");

const paragiha = $(selection);

shell.setTextDirection(SWT.RIGHT_TO_LEFT);

/* function kewud(message, options) creates a dialog with 4 buttons:
"Replace Documentation" & "Append to Documentation" &
"Create Assessment" & "Cancel" (automatically added)

Return Values Explained:
When dialog.open() returns:
0 for first button >> ("Replace Documentation")
1 for second button >> ("Append to Documentation")
2 for third button >> ("Create Assessment")
3 for "Cancel" button

The function then transforms these:
return result == options.length ? null : (result + 1).toString();

So:
0 becomes "1" >> (Replace Documentation)
1 becomes "2" >> (Append Documentation)
2 becomes "3" >> (Create Assessment)
3 (Cancel) becomes null

Why 0 isn't handled: Because the code checks for specific values:
if (updateDocumentation == "3") {
    // Create Assessment
} 
else if (updateDocumentation == "2") {
    // Append Documentation
}
else if (updateDocumentation == "1") {
    // Replace Documentation
}

0 isn't possible because the function adds 1 to all results. If Cancel is clicked (result = 3),
it returns null, which doesn't match any conditions and effectively does nothing. */
function kewud(message, options) {
  const tmpShell = new org.eclipse.swt.widgets.Shell(
    shell,
    org.eclipse.swt.SWT.DIALOG_TRIM |
      org.eclipse.swt.SWT.APPLICATION_MODAL |
      org.eclipse.swt.SWT.RIGHT_TO_LEFT
  );

  var dialog = new org.eclipse.jface.dialogs.MessageDialog(
    tmpShell, // parent global shell
    "تجزیه‌وتحلیل اِلمان انتخاب‌شده", // dialog title
    img, //SWT’s Image constructor treats relative paths relative to the JVM working directory, so we put it next to the script
    message, // message to display
    org.eclipse.jface.dialogs.MessageDialog.QUESTION, // dialog type (QUESTION == 3)
    options.concat(["لغو"]), // buttons array
    0 // default button index
  );

  var result = dialog.open();
  return result == options.length ? null : (result + 1).toString();
}

const dasView = $(selection).filter("archimate-diagram-model");
